WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
Chlorine and iodine belong to
the same family of elements.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.410
Add chlorine to a solution
of potassium iodide,

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.590
and iodine is pushed out.

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.730
Chlorine has taken its place.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.630
Now try it the other way round.

6
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.810
Add iodine to a solution
of potassium chloride,

7
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.730
and nothing happens at all.

8
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.510
Same family, same kind of reaction.

9
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.070
So why does it only work one way?

10
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.250
In this mission, you'll
meet the halogens,

11
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.140
and see how they react
by gaining an electron.

12
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.890
You'll find out how their
reactivity changes down the group,

13
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.490
and how displacement
reveals the order.

14
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.130
And you'll see why the
noble gases don't react.

15
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.610
Your mission: explain why
displacement only goes one way.
